# Upstream Yocto layer repos and pinned revisions for WendyOS.
#
# Sourced by:
#   - bootstrap.sh         (per-build clone into ${PROJECT_DIR}/repos/)
#
# The poky monolith has been retired here; "poky" is composed at clone time
# from three split-style upstream repos (bitbake, openembedded-core,
# meta-yocto). Each board resolves to a layer tree on disk via
# WENDYOS_LAYER_TREE; clones live under repos/${WENDYOS_LAYER_TREE}/<folder>.
#
# A per-board conf/template/boards/<board-id>/repos.overrides file may
# override any URL_*/SRCREV_* below (and WENDYOS_LAYER_TREE) before
# bootstrap.sh builds repos[].

# Layer-tree namespace under repos/. Boards on the same yocto series share
# clones; switching series (or running an isolated experimental tree) means
# pointing at a different tree. Every board is on blacksail, so that is the
# default; a per-board repos.overrides may unconditionally set something else
# (e.g. "wrynose", or "thor-experimental" for an isolated checkout).
WENDYOS_LAYER_TREE="${WENDYOS_LAYER_TREE:-blacksail}"

# Split-poky composition, plus the BSP and add-on layers.
URL_BITBAKE="https://git.openembedded.org/bitbake"
URL_OECORE="https://git.openembedded.org/openembedded-core"
URL_METAYOCTO="https://git.yoctoproject.org/meta-yocto"
URL_OE="https://github.com/openembedded/meta-openembedded.git"
URL_TEGRA="https://github.com/OE4T/meta-tegra.git"
URL_TEGRA_COMM="https://github.com/OE4T/meta-tegra-community"
URL_VIRT="https://git.yoctoproject.org/meta-virtualization.git"
URL_RPI="https://github.com/agherzan/meta-raspberrypi.git"
URL_QCOM="https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/meta-qcom.git"
URL_SECURITY="https://git.yoctoproject.org/meta-security"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The blacksail pin set.
#
# Every board builds on blacksail and shares one clone per layer under
# repos/blacksail/, so these values are the fleet-wide truth. A board file
# should override a pin only when the difference is genuinely board-specific.
# scripts/check-repo-pins.sh checks that boards on one tree never disagree about
# a layer they both use. Run it by hand after changing a pin — nothing in CI
# calls it yet.
#
# Re-pinned 2026-10-23 to Yocto 6.1 "blacksail" (released 2026-09-29). Every
# layer below declares blacksail at its pin, so the compatibility bridges in
# the bblayers and local.conf includes are no longer needed. They are removed
# in a following step of this change. The set has to move as one piece:
# blacksail oe-core sets LAYERSERIES_CORENAMES = "blacksail" only, so an older
# layer that does not declare blacksail stops parsing.
#
# Where a layer has a blacksail release branch, we pin its head, not the
# yocto-6.1 tag. The branch adds only stable-release fixes on top of the tag
# (CVE patches and point upgrades). Release-branch heads stay reachable, so an
# upstream rebase cannot leave a pin dangling.

# Split-poky on blacksail: oe-core and meta-yocto follow their blacksail
# branches. bitbake follows its 2.20 branch, whose head is the yocto-6.1 tag
# (2.20.0, >= oe-core's BB_MIN_VERSION 2.19.1).
SRCREV_BITBAKE="634f8dede6b9d71b5a6691499fd05a8678b46eae"
SRCREV_OECORE="a4461e117c1c501b7021d20c1380e4187fcda4c1"
SRCREV_METAYOCTO="d0119aa2eb77b985fcd33ac527d5c0287eb68e58"

# meta-openembedded blacksail branch.
SRCREV_OE="a9d69bc066bf9498397db27902c287dd666fdfd4"

# meta-virtualization master. It has no blacksail branch; master declares
# LAYERSERIES_COMPAT = "wrynose blacksail".
SRCREV_VIRT="7b0154418de3350fd23a0bd868742f2b570b24d3"

# meta-tegra blacksail branch (JetPack 7.2.1 / L4T R39.2.1, Thor plus the Orin
# family). OE4T names one branch per Yocto release, and that branch carries
# the main L4T release for it. Its master-l4t-rXX branches carry an extra L4T
# release next to it, so no master-l4t-r39.2.x branch is expected.
SRCREV_TEGRA="7bcb209e2b5fbf6619b6f1b391217b5b5242bf13"

# meta-tegra-community blacksail branch.
SRCREV_TEGRA_COMM="92dea1513e64508c047bdd823c7f5febd82384cd"

# meta-raspberrypi master. It has no blacksail branch; master declares
# blacksail. Pinned for reproducibility, since master moves.
SRCREV_RPI="863444d39c9cab81007acc2adad5181dc6bf8f09"

# meta-security master, for meta-tpm (libtss2 + tpm2-tools/tss). Layered on x86
# and every Tegra board (see bblayers/x86.inc and bblayers/tegra-base.inc), so
# it is cloned for all boards, like meta-tegra and meta-raspberrypi. It has no
# blacksail branch; master declares blacksail.
SRCREV_SECURITY="663084f075b98a4b91d86ca0d254a7a7bf1fd0e0"

# meta-qcom master, layered only by the dragonwing and arduino boards. It has
# no blacksail branch; master declares blacksail.
SRCREV_QCOM="93812b537239840bca2f482f61d6a807bea41853"
